--TEST--
a request answers the client address its carrier holds `rule:http-server/trusted-proxies-is-empty-and-empty-reads-nothing` `rule:security/tainted-sources`
--CLIENT_IP--
203.0.113.7
--SCHEME--
https
--HEADERS--
Host: example.test
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `--CLIENT_IP--` is the address the trusted-proxy walk settled on, which a
// case states outright because it is an answer rather than a header: a served
// request reaches the same carrier field through
// `rule:http-server/trusted-proxies-is-empty-and-empty-reads-nothing`'s walk at
// the door, and nothing a program can call re-derives it.
echo Core\Request::clientIp() ?? "none", "\n";
// The three arrive together, one walk having answered the first two: a carrier
// holding half a peer would answer one of them for this request and one for
// whatever set the other.
echo Core\Request::scheme(), "\n";
echo Core\Request::host() ?? "none", "\n";
--EXPECT--
203.0.113.7
https
example.test
